  "claim": "Proved by hand: through a three-edge cut a lower level's unsatisfiable class offers the upper level the replaced line (a contradiction becomes a constraint, and a point crosses levels); through a parity name it offers nothing, and each level keeps its own forced dissonance: two readings of layers. Computed on seven lower-level spaces and two namings: D and N1 held; names carry class-dependent correlations in 41 of 69 satisfiable class readings, including single excluded patterns, which no cut can offer.",
